# The kernel reads a script's shebang literally. A CRLF ending turns
# "#!/bin/sh" into a request for "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist, and the
# failure surfaces as "binary 'semgrep' not found on host" even though the
# file is present and executable -- `command -v` finds it, exec'ing it does
# not. This only appears when the tree is checked out or archived on Windows
# with core.autocrlf=true, so Linux CI builds never reproduce it.
#
# Pin every file that is executed by path to LF, regardless of platform.
backend/api/docker-bin/* text eol=lf
backend/hook/bin/*       text eol=lf
*.sh                     text eol=lf
Dockerfile*              text eol=lf
